//! Flat storage `flat_sub` of table `sub` (generated by GenDB, gendb-flat-storage-v1; not author code).
//!
//! Every column of the table as a plain typed array in source row order: stored row `i` is source row `i`. One
//! part per column, two for a text column (offsets, bytes), in column order. No sorting, partitioning, index,
//! permutation, compression, dictionary or skip metadata. The element type follows the declared SQL type only:
//! bigint I64; integer I32; date I32 days since 1970-01-01; numeric(p,s) I128 coefficient (value =
//! coefficient * 10^-s); text, varchar and char I64 offsets (rows + 1, positions in the bytes part, the first not
//! necessarily 0) and U8 UTF-8 bytes, value `i` = bytes[offsets[i] .. offsets[i + 1]].
//!
//! `represents(parts, rels)`: `rels` is the one stored table and its row `i` is `row_at(parts, i)`. The readers
//! read extents through `StoredParts` and state what they return in terms of `rels`.
//!
//! A nullable column has one more part after its value part(s): its validity, U8, one byte per row. Row `i` of
//! the column is SQL NULL exactly when its validity byte is 0; then its value bytes mean nothing. Its value
//! readers state the value of every row that is not NULL; `read_<column>_validity` states which rows are NULL.
//!
//! Parts:
//!    0 ADSH_OFFSETS: adsh (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!    1 ADSH_BYTES: adsh (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!    2 CIK: cik (integer), I32 value
//!    3 NAME_OFFSETS: name (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!    4 NAME_BYTES: name (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!    5 SIC: sic (integer), I32 value
//!    6 SIC_VALIDITY: sic (integer), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!    7 COUNTRYBA_OFFSETS: countryba (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!    8 COUNTRYBA_BYTES: countryba (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!    9 COUNTRYBA_VALIDITY: countryba (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   10 STPRBA_OFFSETS: stprba (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   11 STPRBA_BYTES: stprba (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   12 STPRBA_VALIDITY: stprba (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   13 CITYBA_OFFSETS: cityba (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   14 CITYBA_BYTES: cityba (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   15 CITYBA_VALIDITY: cityba (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   16 COUNTRYINC_OFFSETS: countryinc (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   17 COUNTRYINC_BYTES: countryinc (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   18 COUNTRYINC_VALIDITY: countryinc (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   19 FORM_OFFSETS: form (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   20 FORM_BYTES: form (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   21 PERIOD: period (integer), I32 value
//!   22 PERIOD_VALIDITY: period (integer), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   23 FY: fy (integer), I32 value
//!   24 FY_VALIDITY: fy (integer), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   25 FP_OFFSETS: fp (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   26 FP_BYTES: fp (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   27 FP_VALIDITY: fp (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   28 FILED: filed (integer), I32 value
//!   29 ACCEPTED_OFFSETS: accepted (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   30 ACCEPTED_BYTES: accepted (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   31 PREVRPT: prevrpt (integer), I32 value
//!   32 NCIKS: nciks (integer), I32 value
//!   33 AFS_OFFSETS: afs (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   34 AFS_BYTES: afs (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   35 AFS_VALIDITY: afs (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   36 WKSI: wksi (integer), I32 value
//!   37 FYE_OFFSETS: fye (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   38 FYE_BYTES: fye (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
//!   39 FYE_VALIDITY: fye (text), U8 validity (0: NULL, otherwise the value part holds the value)
//!   40 INSTANCE_OFFSETS: instance (text), I64 offsets (rows + 1) into the bytes part
//!   41 INSTANCE_BYTES: instance (text), U8 UTF-8 bytes
